-- title:
--   Kernel ideal of an intermediate quotient, coprime case
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic a prime $q'$, algebraic over $\mathbb{Z}/q'$. Let $X_1$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ all of whose $\kappa$-points killed by $q'$ vanish. Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ be such that $\mathbb{H}=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ satisfies `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`: $a<0$, $b<0$, and for each height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ the completion $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division ring exactly when $q'\in v$. Let $\Lambda_1\subseteq\mathbb{H}$ be a maximal order (a finitely generated $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule containing $1$, closed under multiplication, spanning $\mathbb{H}$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, and maximal among such), and let $\theta_1$ be an injective ring map from the subring `rationalEndSubring` generated by the $\kappa$-rational homomorphisms $X_1\to X_1$ (those that are $0$ or given off a finite set by quotients of bivariate polynomials) into $\mathbb{H}$, with image exactly $\Lambda_1$. For a unit $y$ of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ write $I_y=$ `ofFiniteIdele` $\Lambda_1\,y$, the set of $z\in\mathbb{H}$ whose image under $\mathrm{includeLeft}$ lies in $y\cdot$ `finiteAdeleBox` $\Lambda_1$, the latter being the additive group generated by the $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda_1$ and $\alpha$ integral at every finite place; and for a homomorphism $\varphi:X_1\to E$ write $I(\varphi)=\theta_1(\,$`kernelIdealSet`$\,)$ for the image under $\theta_1$ of the set of elements of `rationalEndSubring` of the form $\rho\circ\varphi$ with $\rho:E\to X_1$ $\kappa$-rational. Given: a unit $x$, an elliptic curve $W$, a nonzero $\kappa$-rational $\chi:X_1\to W$ and $d\in\mathbb{H}^\times$ with $I(\chi)=\overline{d\cdot I_x}$ (bar denoting `star`); a natural number $L$ with $q'\nmid L$, a unit $m'$, an elliptic curve $W'$ and $\kappa$-rational $\psi:W\to W'$, $\psi':W'\to W$ with $\psi'\circ\psi=L$ and $\psi\circ\psi'=L$, such that $I(\psi\circ\chi)=\overline{d\cdot I_{xm'}}$; a divisor $M$ of $L$ with $M$ and $L/M$ coprime; a unit $m''$ with $m''$, $m''^{-1}m'$, $M\,m''^{-1}$ and $(L/M)\,m'^{-1}m''$ all in `finiteAdeleBox` $\Lambda_1$; and an elliptic curve $V$ with $\kappa$-rational $\pi:W\to V$ whose kernel is exactly $(L/M)\cdot\ker\psi$ and which is universal in the sense that every $\kappa$-rational $\alpha:W\to V'$ to an elliptic curve with $\ker\pi\le\ker\alpha$ factors as $\alpha=\beta\circ\pi$ with $\beta:V\to V'$ $\kappa$-rational. Then $I(\pi\circ\chi)=\overline{d\cdot I_{xm''}}$.
--
--   This is the arithmetic core of the Deuring–Eichler dictionary between $\kappa$-rational homomorphisms out of a supersingular curve and locally principal right ideals of a maximal order in the definite quaternion algebra ramified exactly at $q'$: it transports a realisation of the class of a finite idele along an intermediate quotient of a cyclic isogeny, in the case where the degree splits into coprime parts. It is used in the construction of the degeneracy maps between supersingular enhanced curves and the class set of an Eichler order, and in the comparison of valuation subrings along the moduli places in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the argument.
